diff --git a/api-ref/source/checkpoint-continuation.inc b/api-ref/source/checkpoint-continuation.inc
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..dcb0280
--- /dev/null
+++ b/api-ref/source/checkpoint-continuation.inc
@@ -0,0 +1,128 @@
+.. -*- rst -*-
+
+Checkpoint continuation (private 3.73)
+======================================
+
+This private fork extension adds a durable grant to the 3.72 checkpoint
+contract. It does not correspond to an upstream API with the same number.
+RPC 3.22 and object manifest 1.41 are required before delegated reserve.
+
+Initial delegation
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+.. rest_method:: POST /v3/{project_id}/checkpoint-operations
+
+The 3.72 request gains two paired fields: ``nova_operation_id`` (canonical
+UUID) and ``allow_service_continuation`` (explicit boolean true). Both may be
+omitted for the original contract. Both are required to create a grant. The
+initial request still requires the project user's token and a verified Nova
+service token. A service-only token cannot reserve or impersonate the actor.
+
+A successful 202 response includes ``continuation`` with ``version=1``,
+``nova_operation_id``, ``owner_project_id``, ``actor_user_id``,
+``executor_service_user_id`` and ``generation=1``. The response has no grant
+mutation API, credentials, connection data or backend references. Exact
+replay returns the same operation; actor/payload changes conflict or are
+not found. Legacy operations cannot gain a grant through replay.
+
+.. literalinclude:: /v3/samples/checkpoint-continuation/checkpoint-create-request.json
+   :language: javascript
+
+.. literalinclude:: /v3/samples/checkpoint-continuation/checkpoint-create-response.json
+   :language: javascript
+
+Service-scoped operation
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+.. rest_method:: GET /v3/checkpoint-service-operations/{nova_operation_id}
+
+The service's own project-scoped token is the primary ``X-Auth-Token``. Its
+subject must match the saved executor, have the service role and be in the
+local allowlist. Original actor/project are selected from the verified grant,
+never from a caller-supplied context. Admin and secondary service identities
+do not bypass the check. A missing or foreign operation returns 404.
+
+All service paths optionally accept ``/v3/{service_project_id}/``. The project
+must be the authenticated service project; it cannot select a tenant owner.
+There is no service collection/list route. GET returns 200 with the same safe
+``checkpoint_operation`` view and continuation binding, including released
+tombstones. A revoked grant cannot be read or continued.
+
+Continue an operation
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+.. rest_method:: POST /v3/checkpoint-service-operations/{nova_operation_id}/action
+
+The body and 202 response follow the 3.72 operation contract: one of execute,
+reconcile, cleanup or release, generation 1, and commit/abort for release.
+Reconcile queries disk results without redispatch. Released operations accept
+only reads; reconcile/cleanup/release retries return 409. Read the tombstone
+to resolve a lost release response.
+
+Read scoped capabilities
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+.. rest_method:: GET /v3/checkpoint-service-operations/{nova_operation_id}/volumes/{volume_id}/capabilities
+
+Returns 200 with the C1 capabilities schema for a volume in the bound set.
+Unbound volumes return 404; no generic tenant-volume query is authorized.
+
+Durable attachment requests
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+.. rest_method:: POST /v3/checkpoint-service-operations/{nova_operation_id}/attachment-requests
+
+The closed body is::
+
+    {"attachment_request": {
+      "id": "<child-uuid>", "generation": 1, "volume_id": "<volume-uuid>",
+      "action": "create", "attachment_id": null,
+      "connector": null, "mountpoint": null
+    }}
+
+All seven fields are required. Actions are create/update/complete/delete.
+Create requires the three nullable fields to be null. Update requires a
+newly created attachment ID and connector, with optional mountpoint.
+Complete/delete require the attachment ID and null connector/mountpoint.
+The instance UUID is taken from the grant. Connector allows host, ip,
+initiator, platform, os_type, nqn, uuid, system uuid, wwpns/wwnns, multipath,
+enforce_multipath and nvme_native_multipath, with their declared types.
+Unknown fields and credentials are rejected with 400.
+
+Response 202 contains ``attachment_request`` with id, operation_id,
+generation, volume_id, action, status, attachment_id and nullable error_code.
+There is no connection_info, connector or schema_version in this REST view.
+Status is prepared, dispatching, pending, succeeded, failed_no_effect or
+unknown. The error code is from a closed safe set, never backend text.
+
+One UUID is accepted for each operation/generation/volume/action. Exact replay
+returns its stored result. Changed payload or a second UUID for the same
+action returns 409. Delete is restricted to original attachments before disk
+revert; reconnect is allowed after every disk step succeeds. Complete requires
+a successful update. The legacy attachment-header bypass is forbidden for a
+delegated operation. Release rejects unfinished attachment requests.
+
+Read an attachment request
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+.. rest_method:: GET /v3/checkpoint-service-operations/{nova_operation_id}/attachment-requests/{child_id}
+
+Returns the same safe result with 200. This is a read, never a new claim or
+backend dispatch. Unknown initialize/terminate results stay unknown without
+backend-specific proof; no universal automatic retry is provided.
+
+Read current attachment data
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+.. rest_method:: GET /v3/checkpoint-service-operations/{nova_operation_id}/attachments/{attachment_id}
+
+Returns 200 with the standard attachment detail fields, including current
+connection_info, for the operation's current original/new attachment. This
+transient response is not copied into the checkpoint journal. Released grants
+cannot read mutable attachment data.
+
+Authentication errors use 401/403; missing or foreign bindings use 404;
+stale generation, unsupported capabilities and state conflicts use 409.
+Initial reserve can also return quota 413 and unavailable backend 503.
+Expiry/revocation is subject to normal Keystone token validation and caching;
+it does not cancel already accepted RPC or backend I/O.
